\newlabel{fig:roche-spring-diagram}{{8}{8}{Roche's original spring-bar analogy: Bar~1 (left) carries a pure primary stress (dead-weight-like load); Bar~2 (centre) carries a pure secondary stress through a soft spring; Bar~3 (right) reproduces the secondary loading through a bolted, effectively rigid connection, producing an intermediate, ``spring effect'' behaviour between Bars~1 and~2}{figure.caption.11}{}}
